The program should have the following features:

- The file name should be passed as a command line argument.
- The results file name should be passed as a command line argument.
- The file should be opened in read-only mode.
- The file should be read into a buffer.
- The buffer should be freed after it is no longer needed.
- The checksum should be calculated for the buffer.
- The number of bytes read should be saved to the results file.
- The checksum should be saved to the results file.

