To prevent buffer overflow, we need to ensure that the buffer size is large enough to hold the string that is being copied into the buffer.

To do this, we can use the `strlen` function to determine the length of the string that is being copied into the buffer. We can then use this length to determine the size of the buffer that we need to allocate.

